# Tor config for ip-relay egress lanes.
#
# IsolateSOCKSAuth is the mechanism the whole Tor provider rests on: tor binds a
# circuit to the SOCKS *username*, so socks5://tor-3g0:x@127.0.0.1:9150 is a
# private egress IP, and changing the username yields a brand-new exit. Without
# this flag every lane would share one circuit and one exit IP.
SocksPort 9150 IsolateSOCKSAuth

DataDirectory /var/lib/tor-ip-relay
Log notice file /var/log/tor-ip-relay.log

# Only the relay talks to this port. Never expose it.
SocksPolicy accept 127.0.0.1/32
SocksPolicy reject *

# Circuits are cheap and we want fresh exits often; a long lifetime just means
# a burned exit lingers in a slot.
MaxCircuitDirtiness 600
NewCircuitPeriod 30

# We only ever egress to opencode.ai over HTTPS. Refusing to be a relay or exit
# for anyone else keeps this node a pure client.
ClientOnly 1
